From: Termux Port <termux@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Fix dynamic library detection for Termux/Android

On Android, shared libraries don't follow the standard Linux naming
convention (libc.so.6). Instead, bionic provides libc.so without
version suffixes. This patch:

1. Handles unversioned .so files (Android/bionic style)
2. Adds $PREFIX/lib to dylib search paths
3. Skips glibc-specific version checks
4. Properly resolves Python extension modules (.cpython-XX-*.so)

--- a/depend/dylib.py
+++ b/depend/dylib.py
@@ -1,3 +1,15 @@
+# ── TERMUX_PATCHED: Fix dylib for Android/bionic ──────────────
+import os as _os
+
+_PREFIX = _os.environ.get("PREFIX", "/data/data/com.termux/files/usr")
+
+# On Android/bionic, shared libs have no version suffix
+# (libc.so, not libc.so.6). Extend the matching patterns.
+_BIONIC_LIBS = {
+    "libc.so", "libm.so", "libdl.so", "libpthread.so",
+    "librt.so", "libutil.so", "libandroid.so", "liblog.so",
+}
+# ── END TERMUX_PATCHED ────────────────────────────────────────
+
